fication of the Casnati–Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus unless those groups are shown to be exactly the obstruction spaces of the CE evaluation map (packet: derive failure from the f_2=5 summand of SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6).\n57\t- `FND-0062` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: On any smooth genus-6 degree-four cover C -> P^1 with balanced splitting F = O(4) ⊕ O(5), the f=4 component of the CE evaluation obstruction bundle \\omega_C \\otimes W_4^\\vee(\\Gamma) has degree -4 for any degree-six divisor \\Gamma, hence H^0(\\omega_C \\otimes W_4^\\vee(\\Gamma)) = 0 and the obstruction vanishes identically on this component.\n58\t- `FND-0063` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: On any smooth genus-6 degree-four cover C -> P^1 with balanced splitting F = O(4) ⊕ O(5), the f=5 component of the CE evaluation obstruction bundle \\omega_C \\otimes W_5^\\vee(\\Gamma) has degree 0 for any degree-six divisor \\Gamma. Consequently, evaluation fails on \\Gamma if and only if O_C(\\Gamma) is isomorphic to L = W_5 \\otimes \\omega_C^{-1}.\n59\t- `FND-0064` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The forgetful map from the relative ordered distinct configuration stack Conf_6(C/B^{bal}) to the relative effective-divisor space of degree six is a finite etale S_6-torsor over the reduced-support open locus.\n60\t- `FND-0067` [corroborated; {'attempt_id': 'ATT-0026', 'campaign_id': 'C66-001', 'subproblem_id': 'C66-GEO-Z'}]: To prove that Z^{bal} is not closed in M_{6,6}, one must exhibit or otherwise establish a closure point in Z minus Z^{bal}. Openness of base-point-freeness/balancedness and one balanced example are insufficient.\n61\t- `FND-0068` [corroborated; {'attempt_id': 'ATT-0026', 'campaign_id': 'C66-001', 'subproblem_id': 'C66-GEO-Z'}]: A degeneracy locus whose component has codimension below the generic determinantal expectation may still be locally cut out by a regular sequence of its actual codimension. A nowhere-lci conclusion requires local ideal-depth or co