okkeeping, so even a corrected strata spectral sequence would be incomplete.\n- `FND-0052` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For the (6,6) CE evaluation-failure locus, the balanced reduced-support relative linear system over the Hurwitz space is an open piece of the failure locus, not a closed pure-codimension-4 subvariety of M_{6,6}; Gysin for (M_{6,6},Z) requires a closed (stratified) embedding after h^0 and splitting-type stratification.\n- `FND-0053` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: That S_6 has rational irreducible representations does not imply that an S_6-cover of a relative configuration/linear-system space carries only Tate local systems; geometric monodromy of the tetragonal family and configuration-space coefficients can still produce non-Tate summands.\n- `FND-0054` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: Declaring the genus-6 balanced tetragonal Hurwitz space ‘rational/Tate’ and deducing pure-Tate cohomology of Z upgrades a predicted/possible motive to an unconditional theorem and is not a substitute for C66-TATE-SUPPORT.\n- `FND-0055` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: Vanishing of H^0(C,ω⊗W_5^∨(Γ)) on the complementary open U does not by itself force W_26 H^{26}(U) (or lowest-weight BM of U) to be pure Tate; CE syzygy vanishing is not a purity theorem for open moduli cohomology.\n- `FND-0057` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: A claimed_complete C66-FULL argument with proof_dependencies=[] and no_undischarged_dependencies=true is inconsistent with the campaign graph requiring GEO-Z→GEO-H0→GEO-COMP→TATE-SUPPORT→TATE-ASSEMBLY before assembly into the exact target.\n- `FND-0058` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: On the balanced tetragonal stack for (g,n)=(6,6), the identification of the CE evaluation-failure locus with a relative P^2-bundle |ω_C(-D)| (fiber dimension exactly 2) requires proof that h^0(ω_C(-D))=1+h^0(D) is constantly 3 on the whole balanced locus, not merely for general tetragonal curve