d; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'generality': 'all g >= 1, n >= 1'}]: The universal determinantal computation underlying C66-GEO-Z is not specific to (g,n) = (6,6). For any g >= 1 and any n >= 1, with Gamma a relative Cartier divisor finite etale of degree n over the base and L_univ = omega_{C_P/P}(Gamma_P) tensor Poin^{-1} on C x_S Pic^0(C/S), one has Fit_0(coker(p_*L_univ -> p_*(L_univ|_{Gamma_P}))) = I_e. Reason: deg L_univ = 2g-2+n > 2g-2 gives R^1p_* = 0 and h^0 = g+n-1; at e the kernel is H^0(omega) of dimension g and the cokernel is H^1(omega) of dimension 1 for EVERY n >= 1, so Hom(ker,coker) has dimension g = dim T_e Pic^0, and the intrinsic derivative is the Serre pairing H^1(O) x H^0(omega) -> H^1(omega), which is perfect. Consequently the (6,6)-specificity of the CE identification enters only through the separate requirement deg N = 2g-2-deg W_5+n = 0, i.e. through the Step-4 identification omega(Gamma) tensor N^{-1} = W_5, and not through the universal Pic^0 lemma at all. This localizes what FND-0074 blocks: the non-transport to neighbouring n is entirely a statement about the failure condition becoming a positive-degree Brill-Noether condition, while the determinantal scheme-structure machinery transports unchanged and can be reused verbatim for other (g,n) whenever the degree-zero condition is arranged.\n- `FND-0097` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'objects': ['balanced tetragonal CE bundle W', 'universal balanced tetragonal stack']}]: The hypothesis that the balanced CE bundle W SPLITS as W_4 + W_5 over the base is removable and should be replaced by the canonical filtration, which matters because the splitting can fail exactly where the campaign wants to use it. On the balanced locus F is fibrewise O(4)+O(5), so the relative Harder-Narasimhan filtration gives a canonical 0 -> L_5 -> F -> L_4 -> 0 over any base; dualizing and twisting yields a canonical 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 with W_4 the degree-20 sub and W_5 the degree-16 quotient. Since